{
  "comment": "Column order of the three tables a Runecraft monolith's OFFERS are built from, from poe-tool-dev/dat-schema (PoE2 entries; its CI republishes schema.min.json on every commit). Offsets are NOT stored - they are arithmetic over the widths in DatColumns, recomputed on load, so a corrected width moves every column after it. THE JOIN: Expedition2Recipes lists each recipe's Runes as an array of Expedition2Runes rows (the rune at index p is what must sit in hole p), its Reward as a BaseItemTypes row (data/item-tables.json carries that table), and its RuneWeights as rows of Expedition2RunesWeights - the table that says at which area level a recipe SHORTER than the monolith may be offered for a given anchor rune at a given slot (RecipeRuneCount, HighlightedRuneSlot, HighlightedRune, MinAreaLevel). The last, unnamed i32 array of Expedition2Recipes (column_19) is the recipe's AREA CONTENT TAGS: on the 0.5.5 HF9 client a recipe carrying any is offered only in an area whose own tag set (AreaInstance.ContentTags in the offsets schema) shares one - one recipe of 322 today, 7SlotAldursLogbook1 with tag 54 (yokkenUA/RunecraftHelper). Named by position because the community schema has not named it; RecipeCatalog reads it by that name. The sizes these columns compute are Expedition2Recipes 201 (0xC9) - the stride RunecraftHelper measured between two live recipe rows - Expedition2Runes 104 (0x68) and Expedition2RunesWeights 57 (0x39); each is checked against the file's own row size when the install is read.",
  "source": "poe-tool-dev/dat-schema, release latest, read 2026-10-06 (schema createdAt 1789458335)",
